=== Adaptor cost: NIST ML-DSA vs the LAS paper's simplified Dilithium ===
build: commit aa71cbf branch report | ML-DSA-87 vs Simplified Dilithium-V (n=8, l=7, kappa=60)
protocol: 5 repetitions x 500 (sign-class) / 1000 (verify-class) iterations, mean +/- SD, same process

--- run-validity gates (a failure invalidates every timing above) ---
rejection gate [simplified Dilithium: Algorithm 1 Sign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.7428 attempts/call (acceptance 36.46%) vs exact theory 2.7186 (36.78%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2162 => OK
rejection gate [simplified Dilithium: Algorithm 2 PreSign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.8180 attempts/call (acceptance 35.49%) vs exact theory 2.7643 (36.18%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2208 => OK
rejection gate [ML-DSA: Sign (matched, no statement)]: 2500 calls, measured 3.9956 attempts/call (acceptance 25.03%) vs FIPS 204 published 3.8500 (25.97%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.3312 => OK
rejection gate [ML-DSA: PreSign (adaptor)]: 2500 calls, measured 3.7752 attempts/call (acceptance 26.49%) vs FIPS 204 published 3.8500 (25.97%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.3312 => OK

